## 12. v24d: manuscript aligned with the current implementation (external review, 6 items)

Scope: text only in paper/stam-m_ja.tex. No implementation, evaluation value, SSOT value, figure PNG, table value or
saved LLM output changed; no LLM call was re-run. Each item below was checked against the code
(scripts/eval_ablation.py, llm/sql_generator.py, llm/schema_linker.py, llm/reranker.py, graph/traversal_engine.py,
safety/sql_validator.py, evaluation/metrics.py, evaluation/metrics_strict.py) and the live DB (36 base tables,
44 FK constraints, 41 undirected graph edges, 82 directed allowed-JOIN conditions).

1. no_dict (documentation mismatch, since the first ablation implementation). The condition empties only the
   schema-mapping dictionary (schema_linker.CONDITION_TABLE_MAP / CONDITION_COLUMN_MAP / map_conditions, 61 entries);
   material_terms.yaml and the condition extractor stay active. Manuscript now says so in the ablation definition,
   Section 4.2 ("スキーマ写像辞書を外すと"), the SchemaGraphSQL comparison and the dictionary-size study: 50/25/10 %
   reduce both dictionaries together, 0 % disables the schema mapping only (identical to no_dict; the term dictionary
   is back to full), so 0 % is not the continuation of 10 %. Table row label "0% (なし)" -> "0% (写像のみ無効)".
   Limitation added: a condition removing both dictionaries was not measured.
2. no_graph (documentation mismatch). eval_ablation passes table_graph=None, join_list=None, all_columns=None, so the
   generator falls back to its fixed 6-table / 25-column / 5-JOIN context (material_entry, composition, structure,
   phase_stability, calculation, calculated_property) and linked tables are restricted to those 6. Manuscript defines
   no_graph as "FK graph + 36-table schema context both removed", and no longer interprets it as the graph alone.
3. Shortest JOIN path (POLICY CHANGE). Before the pipeline integration (commit 07a7a976) the evaluation driver put the
   greedy shortest-path ON conditions first in the allowed-JOIN list. In the current sql_pipeline the result of
   generate_joins_for_tables() only decides whether the required tables are connected; the prompt receives every FK
   edge touching a required table, in both directions (e.g. 38 conditions for material_entry/composition/structure/
   phase_stability versus 3 shortest-path JOINs), and the prompt forbids JOINs outside that list. Section title
   "FKグラフ上の貪欲最短経路JOIN制約" -> "FKグラフによるJOIN制約"; Figure 1 caption, supplement Algorithm S1 (caption
   and preamble: path P is used for the connectivity check, not as a generation constraint), "P を SQL JOIN 句に変換"
   removed, SchemaGraphSQL comparison (2) reworded.
4. n-best (documentation mismatch, implementation unchanged since 48692511). GPT-5.5 is called n times (default 3)
   independently with the same input; a rule-based SQL is added as a candidate when available; each candidate gets a
   mechanical score (SQLGuard pass, trial execution, non-empty result, condition coverage, row-count plausibility);
   final ranking = 0.6 mechanical + 0.4 GPT-5.5 semantic score; top-1 is used. no_nbest (n=1) skips the whole
   multi-candidate path (scoring, rule-based candidate, reranker selection).
5. SQLGuard (documentation mismatch). validate_sql() distinguishes rejected (errors) / warning / modified. Of the 15
   checks, 12 reject (multiple statements, forbidden keywords, SELECT-only, dangerous functions, system tables,
   CTE-body SELECT-only, tautology, allowed tables, allowed columns, subquery depth, function allowlist, complexity
   budget), 2 warn only (non-FK JOIN, arithmetic column types; the SQL still executes) and 1 rewrites (LIMIT added
   when missing / capped when too large). Each item in the main text and the supplement list is tagged
   ［棄却］/［警告］/［書き換え］. "いずれかの検査に通らないSQLは棄却" and the "SELECT * 禁止" claim were removed.
6. Common-column projection (metric-definition limitation, already partly disclosed). Recall, Precision, F1 and the
   lenient common-column exact are all computed on cols(gen) ∩ cols(gold), so a missing required gold column is not
   detected by any of them; only the strict exact result-set match (column list + typed rows) and the require-all
   scoring-policy column (Table S20) detect it. Stated explicitly in Section 2.1.3 with references.
Additional: no_reranker disables both rerank_sql_candidates and rerank_schema_tables (schema-link table reordering in the
schema-linking section) while the local cross-encoder for few-shot example selection stays active; stated in the ablation
definition.

